{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-3-antisymm","title":"lem:dc-ch0-5-3-antisymm","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds.md","line":300,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds.tex#lem:dc-ch0-5-3-antisymm","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-2]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch0-5-3-antisymm","line":711,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[antisymmetry of the bracket]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch0-5-3-antisymm}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch0-5-2}\n\n  \\dcref{ch0:5.3}\n  For differentiable vector fields $X$ and $Y$ one has $[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  By the defining identity of \\cref{lem:dc-ch0-5-2},\n  $[X,Y]f=XYf-YXf$ and $[Y,X]f=YXf-XYf$ for every differentiable function $f$.\n  Hence $[X,Y]f=-[Y,X]f$ for all such $f$, and uniqueness in\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch0-5-2} gives $[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[antisymmetry of the bracket] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368302d352d332d616e746973796d6d\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh00_DifferentiableManifolds%23lem%3Adc-ch0-5-2\">↗ lem:dc-ch0-5-2</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch0:5.3</span></span>For differentiable vector fields <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Y$\">$Y$</span> one has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$\">$[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>By the defining identity of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh00_DifferentiableManifolds%23lem%3Adc-ch0-5-2\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-2\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368302d352d32\">section 4</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[X,Y]f=XYf-YXf$\">$[X,Y]f=XYf-YXf$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[Y,X]f=YXf-XYf$\">$[Y,X]f=YXf-XYf$</span> for every differentiable function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>. Hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[X,Y]f=-[Y,X]f$\">$[X,Y]f=-[Y,X]f$</span> for all such <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>, and uniqueness in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh00_DifferentiableManifolds%23lem%3Adc-ch0-5-2\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-2\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368302d352d32\">section 4</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$\">$[X,Y]=-[Y,X]$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-2-smooth","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-3-jacobi","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch00_DifferentiableManifolds#lem:dc-ch0-5-2","title":"lem:dc-ch0-5-2","label":"lem:dc-ch0-5-2"}],"backli